1
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,000
"Connecting to You."

2
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:21,208
Wu Da-Wei, wake up.

3
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:23,957
Ten more minutes.

4
00:01:23,958 --> 00:01:24,999
No way.

5
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,707
We're going to be late in ten minutes.

6
00:01:26,708 --> 00:01:27,500
Get up.

7
00:01:27,501 --> 00:01:28,874
You lazy pig.

8
00:01:28,875 --> 00:01:29,875
Hurry up.

9
00:01:30,083 --> 00:01:31,708
The sun's already up.

10
00:01:32,708 --> 00:01:34,208
Then five more minutes.

11
00:01:35,250 --> 00:01:37,750
No. If we're late,
the landlord's gonna get mad.

12
00:01:38,250 --> 00:01:39,499
Please.

13
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:42,540
I've been on night shifts
and overtime all week.

14
00:01:42,541 --> 00:01:44,749
Your lease is up in two months.

15
00:01:44,750 --> 00:01:46,500
Aren't you worried at all?

16
00:01:48,250 --> 00:01:49,250
It's fine.

17
00:01:50,625 --> 00:01:51,625
Cockroach!

18
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,208
Where?

19
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Got you.

20
00:02:01,625 --> 00:02:02,832
What do you mean?

21
00:02:02,833 --> 00:02:03,833
You…

22
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,000
No, no.

23
00:02:06,166 --> 00:02:12,583
(The Thirteenth Line | The Principle
of Scarcity: Connecting to You)

24
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:15,750
Thank God the landlord is late.

25
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,458
Mm.

26
00:02:19,875 --> 00:02:22,999
Sorry, sorry, there was traffic on the way.

27
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,040
We just got here too.

28
00:02:24,041 --> 00:02:25,041
Okay.

29
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:29,125
Take your time.

30
00:02:35,375 --> 00:02:36,958
Sorry, give me a second.

31
00:02:42,750 --> 00:02:43,874
Sorry.

32
00:02:43,875 --> 00:02:45,250
The door's stuck.

33
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:47,625
Give me a second.

34
00:02:48,375 --> 00:02:50,083
Or maybe we should…

35
00:02:50,875 --> 00:02:51,999
reschedule.

36
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,249
I'll be quick,

37
00:02:53,250 --> 00:02:54,125
just wait a second.

38
00:02:54,126 --> 00:02:55,250
It's okay.

39
00:02:56,944 --> 00:02:57,986
Hey...!

40
00:02:58,125 --> 00:02:59,749
We're meeting the
landlord for the first time,

41
00:02:59,750 --> 00:03:00,999
and there's already a blue line.

42
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:02,125
How is that possible?

43
00:03:02,375 --> 00:03:04,458
Maybe she's the reason?

44
00:03:04,875 --> 00:03:06,124
Maybe there's something about the place

45
00:03:06,125 --> 00:03:07,500
that she's not telling us.

46
00:03:07,750 --> 00:03:08,875
Let me check.

47
00:03:09,125 --> 00:03:11,208
There are plenty of dishonest landlords.

48
00:03:12,375 --> 00:03:13,375
Wow, there really is.

49
00:03:13,750 --> 00:03:15,832
She's had two lawsuits before,

50
00:03:15,833 --> 00:03:17,125
both against her tenants.

51
00:03:17,875 --> 00:03:19,458
Good thing you caught it in time.

52
00:03:22,625 --> 00:03:24,250
Is that work-related?

53
00:03:25,250 --> 00:03:25,875
Yeah.

54
00:03:25,876 --> 00:03:28,374
There's an issue with a
case I need to transfer,

55
00:03:28,375 --> 00:03:30,708
so I might have to go
back to the station later.

56
00:03:31,291 --> 00:03:33,375
Do you want to head
back first and deal with it?

57
00:03:34,250 --> 00:03:36,332
But we still have to see one more place.

58
00:03:36,333 --> 00:03:37,499
It's fine. You go ahead.

59
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:39,958
I can check it myself.

60
00:03:40,750 --> 00:03:42,000
Are you sure?

61
00:03:42,375 --> 00:03:43,375
It's okay.

62
00:03:44,125 --> 00:03:45,250
Alright then.

63
00:03:54,625 --> 00:03:55,500
Excuse me,

64
00:03:55,625 --> 00:03:57,249
are you Mrs. Hsiao?

65
00:03:57,250 --> 00:03:59,332
Are you Lin, here to see the place?

66
00:03:59,333 --> 00:04:00,083
Yes.

67
00:04:00,084 --> 00:04:01,499
Just call me Shanshan.

68
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:02,874
The house is in the alley.

69
00:04:02,875 --> 00:04:04,124
I'll take you.

70
00:04:04,125 --> 00:04:05,000
Okay.

71
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,000
This way.

72
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:08,624
Let me just give you a quick background.

73
00:04:08,625 --> 00:04:09,375
So, for this apartment,

74
00:04:09,376 --> 00:04:12,124
after the last tenant moved out,
I renovated the place,

75
00:04:12,125 --> 00:04:14,333
so everything's in great condition.

76
00:04:14,375 --> 00:04:14,750
Okay.

77
00:04:14,750 --> 00:04:15,750
It's here.

78
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:23,583
And here is…

79
00:04:27,875 --> 00:04:29,375
Why do you only have one line?

80
00:04:30,875 --> 00:04:32,125
You can see it too?

81
00:04:34,791 --> 00:04:35,750
Yeah.

82
00:04:35,750 --> 00:04:36,750
So your line with your boyfriend

83
00:04:36,751 --> 00:04:38,833
has been silver-gray from the start?

84
00:04:38,875 --> 00:04:39,625
Yeah.

85
00:04:39,875 --> 00:04:43,874
I've never seen a line
like that on anyone else.

86
00:04:43,875 --> 00:04:46,708
That means your
connection is pretty special.

87
00:04:49,250 --> 00:04:50,375
To me,

88
00:04:50,750 --> 00:04:52,375
he really is someone special.

89
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:53,707
When I say special,

90
00:04:53,708 --> 00:04:54,908
I don't mean it in a good way.

91
00:04:55,875 --> 00:04:57,583
Then what does it mean?

92
00:04:59,125 --> 00:05:00,874
I've met a few people like that before,

93
00:05:00,875 --> 00:05:01,999
people with only one line.

94
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:03,749
Their relationships always ended

95
00:05:03,750 --> 00:05:06,500
in a really destructive way.

96
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:09,374
I'm not trying to scare you.

97
00:05:09,375 --> 00:05:10,875
It's just the truth.

98
00:05:11,375 --> 00:05:13,875
Like this one girl I met five years ago,

99
00:05:14,125 --> 00:05:15,999
she was super possessive,

100
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:19,333
and even tried to die together with
her boyfriend. Luckily it didn't happen.

101
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:21,999
There was another guy

102
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:23,874
who ended up being really toxic.

103
00:05:23,875 --> 00:05:26,375
His partner got serious depression.

104
00:05:28,750 --> 00:05:32,374
But Da-Wei and I aren't that emotional.

105
00:05:32,375 --> 00:05:33,999
You guys just started seeing each other,

106
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,624
so it's still hard to tell.

107
00:05:35,625 --> 00:05:38,375
You'll know with time.

108
00:05:39,125 --> 00:05:40,749
Is that so?

109
00:05:40,750 --> 00:05:41,875
Yeah.

110
00:05:45,625 --> 00:05:46,625
Shanshan,

111
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:48,625
then what should I do?

112
00:05:49,375 --> 00:05:51,916
Keep your distance.

113
00:05:57,750 --> 00:05:59,458
Dinner's here.

114
00:05:59,875 --> 00:06:02,083
What, you only care about the food?

115
00:06:02,375 --> 00:06:04,125
You're treating me like a delivery guy.

116
00:06:04,375 --> 00:06:06,250
Well, this delivery guy's pretty good.

117
00:06:06,375 --> 00:06:07,416
Deserves a tip.

118
00:06:07,750 --> 00:06:09,000
How much?

119
00:06:10,750 --> 00:06:13,000
Did you finish your work stuff?

120
00:06:13,125 --> 00:06:15,208
Yeah, pretty much.

121
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:15,958
What about you?

122
00:06:15,959 --> 00:06:17,833
How was the last place?

123
00:06:19,250 --> 00:06:21,125
I didn't find anything I liked.

124
00:06:21,458 --> 00:06:22,458
Oh.

125
00:06:22,458 --> 00:06:23,458
Yeah.

126
00:06:23,583 --> 00:06:24,624
It's okay.

127
00:06:24,625 --> 00:06:25,625
I'm off in a few days.

128
00:06:25,626 --> 00:06:27,499
I already scheduled two more places to see.

129
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:28,458
In between,

130
00:06:28,459 --> 00:06:31,000
how about we go watch a movie together?

131
00:06:35,958 --> 00:06:37,625
You finally have a day off.

132
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,249
You don't have to spend
all your time with me.

133
00:06:40,250 --> 00:06:41,500
Have you been wanting to

134
00:06:41,750 --> 00:06:44,250
meet up with any friends lately?

135
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:46,625
You can use that time to do that.

136
00:06:50,375 --> 00:06:51,375
Not really.

137
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,708
It's okay, just think about it.

138
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,374
I'm going to the bathroom.

139
00:06:55,375 --> 00:06:56,375
Okay.

140
00:07:09,875 --> 00:07:11,035
I'm seriously getting fed up.

141
00:07:12,125 --> 00:07:13,125
What's wrong?

142
00:07:13,375 --> 00:07:16,957
Let me tell you, there's this guy
lately who's super annoying and stupid.

143
00:07:16,958 --> 00:07:17,999
I get annoyed the moment I see him.

144
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,249
Help me check the line.

145
00:07:19,250 --> 00:07:20,374
What kind of karmic connection
do I even have with him?

146
00:07:20,375 --> 00:07:21,375
That guy.

147
00:07:24,333 --> 00:07:25,499
Isn't that Nan?

148
00:07:25,500 --> 00:07:26,624
Exactly.

149
00:07:26,625 --> 00:07:27,583
So annoying. I hate him.

150
00:07:27,584 --> 00:07:29,749
He's always hanging around me,

151
00:07:29,750 --> 00:07:31,249
telling stupid jokes,

152
00:07:31,250 --> 00:07:32,625
doing a bunch of stupid things.

153
00:07:32,875 --> 00:07:34,499
Or you could just touch the line

154
00:07:34,500 --> 00:07:36,000
and tell me what he's thinking.

155
00:07:37,458 --> 00:07:38,999
I don't think that's necessary.

156
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,250
I can kind of tell already.

157
00:07:41,375 --> 00:07:42,958
Don't get mad yet.

158
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,833
I'll go talk to him for you.

159
00:07:45,625 --> 00:07:48,625
Actually, Nan's jokes are
kind of funny sometimes, right?

160
00:07:49,750 --> 00:07:51,541
Don't you think?

161
00:07:51,750 --> 00:07:54,750
I meant well.

162
00:07:55,875 --> 00:07:59,708
I knew Xiao-Yu's been
stressed about exams lately,

163
00:08:02,250 --> 00:08:04,708
so I thought I'd surprise her.

164
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:07,125
But I didn't expect her hot Americano

165
00:08:07,625 --> 00:08:09,583
to spill into her bag.

166
00:08:09,625 --> 00:08:11,000
I tried to catch it

167
00:08:11,250 --> 00:08:13,000
and ended up burning my hands too.

168
00:08:14,208 --> 00:08:15,583
Don't touch it, it hurts.

169
00:08:16,125 --> 00:08:17,125
That bad?

170
00:08:18,875 --> 00:08:20,458
Was Xiao-Yu really mad?

171
00:08:24,750 --> 00:08:25,750
Stop talking.

172
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:29,082
- I didn't do anything.
- I said stop.

173
00:08:29,083 --> 00:08:30,624
I thought Xiao-Yu

174
00:08:30,625 --> 00:08:32,625
and I were getting along better lately.

175
00:08:33,125 --> 00:08:35,333
I thought maybe we could
get to know each other better.

176
00:08:37,250 --> 00:08:38,750
Guess that's not happening now.

177
00:08:39,625 --> 00:08:41,250
Yeah, no chance.

178
00:08:43,250 --> 00:08:45,874
I've got something to do, I'm heading out.

179
00:08:45,875 --> 00:08:47,374
You're leaving?

180
00:08:47,375 --> 00:08:49,458
Didn't you say you didn't
want to hear me talk?

181
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,249
Fine.

182
00:08:52,250 --> 00:08:53,999
So now you just believe whatever I say?

183
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:54,833
No, it's just…

184
00:08:54,834 --> 00:08:56,750
I have dinner plans with Da-Wei.

185
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:58,499
Da-Wei… again.

186
00:08:58,500 --> 00:08:59,500
Alright.

187
00:08:59,501 --> 00:09:03,624
Anyway, baking soda with
warm water removes coffee stains.

188
00:09:03,625 --> 00:09:05,457
Go clean her stuff first.

189
00:09:05,458 --> 00:09:06,750
We'll talk later.

190
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:09,000
Okay.

191
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,500
Don't look.

192
00:09:17,750 --> 00:09:19,374
Peeking is the start of being controlling.

193
00:09:19,375 --> 00:09:21,125
Don't look.

194
00:09:30,625 --> 00:09:32,458
Hurry up and eat, it's getting cold.

195
00:09:32,750 --> 00:09:33,833
I was just thinking

196
00:09:34,625 --> 00:09:35,958
we could eat together.

197
00:09:38,458 --> 00:09:41,000
I saw two places today, take a look.

198
00:09:41,833 --> 00:09:42,833
Okay.

199
00:09:46,625 --> 00:09:47,833
Keep your distance.

200
00:09:49,750 --> 00:09:50,750
I think

201
00:09:51,125 --> 00:09:54,458
the first place feels a bit cramped.

202
00:09:55,625 --> 00:09:56,625
Really?

203
00:09:56,750 --> 00:09:59,375
And the second one seems kind of remote.

204
00:09:59,625 --> 00:10:02,250
I heard transportation there isn't great.

205
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:04,583
Let me see.

206
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:12,500
I'm thinking maybe

207
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,625
we don't need to rush finding a place.

208
00:10:17,875 --> 00:10:19,375
We can wait if needed.

209
00:10:19,750 --> 00:10:20,832
But weren't you the one

210
00:10:20,833 --> 00:10:23,000
who keeps reminding
me my lease is almost up?

211
00:10:23,875 --> 00:10:25,500
Yeah, I was.

212
00:10:26,125 --> 00:10:29,124
It's just that after looking around,

213
00:10:29,125 --> 00:10:31,124
finding a place that works for both of us

214
00:10:31,125 --> 00:10:32,874
isn't that easy.

215
00:10:32,875 --> 00:10:35,249
Maybe we should take it slow.

216
00:10:35,250 --> 00:10:37,499
You could also look for a studio.

217
00:10:37,500 --> 00:10:38,999
I can renew my place with Nan

218
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,333
for now.

219
00:10:42,375 --> 00:10:43,458
Alright.

220
00:10:44,125 --> 00:10:46,833
Let's keep looking then.

221
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,499
That's good.

222
00:10:55,500 --> 00:10:58,875
Putting off moving in together
like this is actually the right move.

223
00:10:59,250 --> 00:11:01,500
You'll both have more personal space.

224
00:11:03,125 --> 00:11:05,500
Even though I'm a bit disappointed
we can't live together,

225
00:11:06,625 --> 00:11:09,708
I still want to maintain this
relationship with Da-Wei.

226
00:11:10,250 --> 00:11:11,375
What should I do?

227
00:11:11,625 --> 00:11:12,458
Here.

228
00:11:12,482 --> 00:11:14,273
Take this first.

229
00:11:16,875 --> 00:11:18,125
What is it?

230
00:11:18,875 --> 00:11:21,624
It's a charm I got from a temple.

231
00:11:21,625 --> 00:11:23,874
Take it home and put it somewhere safe.

232
00:11:23,875 --> 00:11:24,999
It'll help you

233
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,375
keep your relationship stable.

234
00:11:28,375 --> 00:11:30,625
But these scissors…

235
00:11:32,083 --> 00:11:33,958
what are they for?

236
00:11:36,500 --> 00:11:38,125
What do you think they're for?!

237
00:11:38,625 --> 00:11:39,958
To cut off your obsession.

238
00:11:41,500 --> 00:11:43,000
- Obsession?
- Yeah.

239
00:11:43,375 --> 00:11:44,000
Obsession.

240
00:11:44,001 --> 00:11:45,582
After you take it home,

241
00:11:45,583 --> 00:11:47,374
put it under your bed.

242
00:11:47,375 --> 00:11:49,750
And remember, don't let it get wet.

243
00:11:50,875 --> 00:11:51,875
Don't let it get wet.

244
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,083
Don't let it get wet.

245
00:11:54,750 --> 00:11:55,750
Don't let it get wet.

246
00:11:56,375 --> 00:11:57,458
Don't let it get wet.

247
00:12:03,416 --> 00:12:04,208
Hello.

248
00:12:04,209 --> 00:12:05,374
Hey.

249
00:12:05,375 --> 00:12:06,375
Where are you?

250
00:12:06,376 --> 00:12:07,833
What's wrong?

251
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:10,082
Chiang Chao-Nan, I'm
doing this for your own good.

252
00:12:10,083 --> 00:12:11,083
Wait a second.

253
00:12:11,084 --> 00:12:13,000
Trust me.

254
00:12:15,125 --> 00:12:16,125
He's here.

255
00:12:17,875 --> 00:12:19,875
Say what you need to
say. My time's valuable.

256
00:12:27,375 --> 00:12:29,375
I've cleaned everything thoroughly.

257
00:12:29,750 --> 00:12:31,249
If you still think there are stains

258
00:12:31,250 --> 00:12:32,750
or any smell,

259
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:34,499
I'll buy you a new one.

260
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:35,999
Whatever.

261
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:38,250
I didn't expect it to be that clean anyway.

262
00:12:39,375 --> 00:12:41,500
Your burn still isn't healed?

263
00:12:43,875 --> 00:12:44,875
Oh.

264
00:12:45,375 --> 00:12:47,208
It's mostly better.

265
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:51,332
It's just this part.

266
00:12:51,333 --> 00:12:52,999
It's still red and it stings.

267
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,124
Everything else is fine.

268
00:12:54,125 --> 00:12:55,250
So ugly.

269
00:12:55,875 --> 00:12:58,749
That's why I hate idiots
like you who act so reckless.

270
00:12:58,750 --> 00:13:00,250
Serves you right.

271
00:13:03,875 --> 00:13:04,999
Go after her.

272
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:06,000
I think she hates me.

273
00:13:07,250 --> 00:13:09,250
That's definitely not what she meant.

274
00:13:09,750 --> 00:13:11,374
That's definitely what she meant.

275
00:13:11,375 --> 00:13:13,207
She said my bandage looks ugly,

276
00:13:13,208 --> 00:13:14,249
called me an idiot,

277
00:13:14,250 --> 00:13:15,749
and said I'm ugly too.

278
00:13:15,750 --> 00:13:17,124
That's definitely hate.

279
00:13:17,125 --> 00:13:19,874
That kind of “hate”
actually means she likes you.

280
00:13:19,875 --> 00:13:21,124
What nonsense are you talking about?

281
00:13:21,125 --> 00:13:22,999
Hate is hate. Like is like.

282
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:25,124
Chiang Chao-Nan, listen.

283
00:13:25,125 --> 00:13:27,624
The line between you
and Xiao-Yu is already pink.

284
00:13:27,625 --> 00:13:30,375
You like her, and she likes you too.

285
00:13:31,125 --> 00:13:32,500
Just go after her.

286
00:13:33,625 --> 00:13:34,874
Trust me.

287
00:13:34,875 --> 00:13:35,625
Pink?

288
00:13:35,626 --> 00:13:37,999
- Yeah.
- No way it's pink.

289
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,500
She said she hates me.

290
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:42,000
You really don't understand girls at all.

291
00:13:42,500 --> 00:13:44,999
Chiang Chao-Nan, hurry up and come to the
infirmary with me to change your dressing.

292
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,166
Do you really want it to get infected?

293
00:13:47,625 --> 00:13:49,750
Can't you tell how Xiao-Yu feels?

294
00:13:51,375 --> 00:13:53,499
Go after her.

295
00:13:53,500 --> 00:13:54,625
I'm coming.

296
00:13:55,938 --> 00:13:57,355
Honey...

297
00:14:00,727 --> 00:14:02,476
This place is really spacious.

298
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:03,500
Yeah.

299
00:14:03,501 --> 00:14:05,874
It's an older building,

300
00:14:05,875 --> 00:14:07,124
so there aren't many shared facilities.

301
00:14:07,125 --> 00:14:10,333
That's why the indoor space is so big.

302
00:14:11,243 --> 00:14:14,076
Sorry, I need to take this call.

303
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:23,208
I think it's pretty nice.

304
00:14:23,500 --> 00:14:24,999
It has the space you like

305
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:26,749
and the good lighting I care about.

306
00:14:26,750 --> 00:14:27,875
What do you think?

307
00:14:29,750 --> 00:14:30,875
I think…

308
00:14:34,250 --> 00:14:37,208
what if I've got another
blue line with the landlord?

309
00:14:38,250 --> 00:14:39,999
We've seen so many places already,

310
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,124
why can't we find a good connection?

311
00:14:42,125 --> 00:14:43,749
Could it be my problem?

312
00:14:43,750 --> 00:14:45,499
You're not the problem.

313
00:14:45,500 --> 00:14:48,583
Your line with the landlord is a yellow
one, meaning a good relationship.

314
00:14:50,375 --> 00:14:51,625
This place seems…

315
00:14:52,625 --> 00:14:54,124
like a haunted house.

316
00:14:54,125 --> 00:14:55,374
- Haunted house?
- This is not a haunted house.

317
00:14:55,375 --> 00:14:56,125
Who said that?

318
00:14:56,126 --> 00:14:57,249
I'll sue them.

319
00:14:57,250 --> 00:14:58,957
Tell me, who said that?

320
00:14:58,958 --> 00:15:00,624
Where did you hear that?

321
00:15:00,625 --> 00:15:02,124
Sir,

322
00:15:02,125 --> 00:15:05,333
that “haunted house”
comment was just a joke.

323
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:07,874
Nobody said anything about
your house being haunted.

324
00:15:07,875 --> 00:15:08,875
Yeah.

325
00:15:08,876 --> 00:15:10,332
We won't say that to anyone either.

326
00:15:10,333 --> 00:15:11,333
Please don't worry.

327
00:15:13,875 --> 00:15:16,458
We're really sorry for upsetting you.

328
00:15:17,125 --> 00:15:18,208
Thank you.

329
00:15:28,750 --> 00:15:30,374
Can you explain to me

330
00:15:30,375 --> 00:15:32,291
why you lied?

331
00:15:37,625 --> 00:15:39,000
Or is this weird behavior

332
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,000
related to this?

333
00:15:41,125 --> 00:15:42,750
Where did you find this?

334
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:44,624
I found it under the bed

335
00:15:44,625 --> 00:15:46,125
when I was cleaning yesterday.

336
00:15:47,125 --> 00:15:49,874
Why does it look like this now?

337
00:15:49,875 --> 00:15:51,155
Because I was mopping the floor.

338
00:15:51,250 --> 00:15:53,333
This thing can't get wet.

339
00:15:54,125 --> 00:15:55,458
You put this there on purpose?

340
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:56,458
Why?

341
00:15:56,459 --> 00:15:58,000
Can you give it back to me first?

342
00:15:58,250 --> 00:15:59,000
Please.

343
00:15:59,001 --> 00:16:01,750
Not until you explain everything.

344
00:16:03,125 --> 00:16:06,416
You forget I'm a cop,
and I will get my answer.

345
00:16:08,375 --> 00:16:09,625
Okay.

346
00:16:10,958 --> 00:16:12,500
Sit down.

347
00:16:20,333 --> 00:16:23,583
Do you remember when I
went to see that place alone?

348
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:26,750
I met the landlord, Shanshan.

349
00:16:27,125 --> 00:16:28,249
She's like me,

350
00:16:28,250 --> 00:16:30,500
she can see the lines between people.

351
00:16:32,875 --> 00:16:35,708
It's the first time
I've met someone with the same ability.

352
00:16:36,125 --> 00:16:37,749
After she saw I only had one line,

353
00:16:37,750 --> 00:16:38,875
she warned me that

354
00:16:39,250 --> 00:16:42,500
people with only one line
tend to be very possessive,

355
00:16:42,750 --> 00:16:45,458
and are more likely to
become toxic partners.

356
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:48,583
Does she have any proof?

357
00:16:49,250 --> 00:16:51,333
She said she's seen
people like that before,

358
00:16:51,375 --> 00:16:53,375
and their relationships never ended well.

359
00:16:53,875 --> 00:16:56,083
So I got scared I might hurt you,

360
00:16:56,625 --> 00:16:58,500
and I asked her for those scissors.

361
00:16:58,750 --> 00:16:59,833
So what do they do?

362
00:17:00,875 --> 00:17:01,999
She said

363
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:03,499
if I put them under your bed,

364
00:17:03,500 --> 00:17:05,624
they can cut away your inner conflict,

365
00:17:05,625 --> 00:17:09,750
so we won't doubt or hurt each other.

366
00:17:10,750 --> 00:17:13,666
So that's why you've
been acting weird lately.

367
00:17:14,125 --> 00:17:15,874
You were worried about hurting me,

368
00:17:15,875 --> 00:17:18,499
and that's why you
started stalling our move.

369
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:19,750
That's the reason too, right?

370
00:17:24,250 --> 00:17:25,750
Okay, I get it.

371
00:17:26,250 --> 00:17:27,583
But I don't believe it.

372
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,874
But don't you believe in my ability?

373
00:17:30,875 --> 00:17:32,125
I believe you.

374
00:17:34,625 --> 00:17:36,124
But I can't see the lines myself,

375
00:17:36,125 --> 00:17:39,583
so I can't judge their changes or meaning.

376
00:17:40,500 --> 00:17:41,957
In the end, I can only
rely on my own feelings

377
00:17:41,958 --> 00:17:43,458
to make decisions in life.

378
00:17:45,208 --> 00:17:48,916
So you don't believe
what Shanshan said either?

379
00:17:50,375 --> 00:17:51,458
It's not that.

380
00:17:53,250 --> 00:17:55,874
I've decided to believe that
we'll get through this together,

381
00:17:55,875 --> 00:17:57,999
build our relationship properly,

382
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,958
and stay together for the long run.

383
00:18:01,125 --> 00:18:03,249
But you're the one who can see the lines,

384
00:18:03,250 --> 00:18:05,125
so I understand why you're worried.

385
00:18:05,375 --> 00:18:06,500
So

386
00:18:08,250 --> 00:18:10,374
if you want to slow things down,

387
00:18:10,375 --> 00:18:12,375
I fully support you.

388
00:18:14,208 --> 00:18:15,625
Thank you.

389
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:18,458
But I'm sorry too.

390
00:18:18,625 --> 00:18:20,208
I was so focused on

391
00:18:21,625 --> 00:18:23,500
the possibility of hurting us.

392
00:18:25,500 --> 00:18:27,458
You're just… a little silly.

393
00:18:27,625 --> 00:18:30,250
That's why you let superstition
mess with your head.

394
00:18:31,375 --> 00:18:32,500
I'm telling you,

395
00:18:32,625 --> 00:18:34,125
I can also help

396
00:18:34,625 --> 00:18:36,749
get rid of those scissors for you.

397
00:18:36,750 --> 00:18:38,625
Stop teasing me.

398
00:18:39,125 --> 00:18:40,999
I just want us to stay
together for a long time.

399
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:42,833
That's why I overthink.

400
00:18:43,375 --> 00:18:46,124
Give me back the scissors.

401
00:18:46,125 --> 00:18:48,250
- Come on.
- Come and get them.

402
00:18:49,375 --> 00:18:50,749
Stop tickling me.

403
00:18:50,750 --> 00:18:51,833
That's evil.

404
00:18:53,250 --> 00:18:54,707
I'm teaching you

405
00:18:54,708 --> 00:18:57,125
how to properly maintain a relationship.

406
00:18:58,875 --> 00:19:00,000
Got it?

407
00:19:00,625 --> 00:19:02,083
A little bit.

408
00:19:06,250 --> 00:19:07,500
Hey, that was sneaky.

409
00:19:09,250 --> 00:19:11,583
It's my secret weapon.

410
00:19:17,250 --> 00:19:17,958
Thanks.

411
00:19:17,958 --> 00:19:18,750
Thanks.

412
00:19:18,751 --> 00:19:20,832
I heard their pork floss
egg is really good too.

413
00:19:20,833 --> 00:19:22,833
Pork floss egg wrap.

414
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:27,083
What a coincidence.

415
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:29,000
Having breakfast together?

416
00:19:30,625 --> 00:19:32,958
When did you two get together?

417
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:37,875
No, I'm just…

418
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:40,375
Recently, just recently.

419
00:19:40,750 --> 00:19:42,083
Well then,

420
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,583
congrats.

421
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:49,375
You two going out for breakfast this early

422
00:19:50,227 --> 00:19:51,476
means...

423
00:19:51,500 --> 00:19:54,333
Xiao-Yu, you were with Nan last night?

424
00:19:54,500 --> 00:19:56,124
Don't get the wrong idea.

425
00:19:56,125 --> 00:19:57,875
We watched a show.

426
00:19:58,250 --> 00:19:59,499
Nothing happened, don't misunderstand.

427
00:19:59,500 --> 00:20:00,333
I'm not that impatient.

428
00:20:00,375 --> 00:20:01,726
No one asked for that much detail.

429
00:20:01,750 --> 00:20:02,375
Seriously.

430
00:20:02,376 --> 00:20:04,583
You should just focus on what to eat.

431
00:20:05,875 --> 00:20:07,375
Looking for a new place?

432
00:20:07,833 --> 00:20:09,673
We're trying to find a
place to live together.

433
00:20:10,250 --> 00:20:11,500
Found one yet?

434
00:20:12,875 --> 00:20:15,208
Finding a good place takes a bit of luck.

435
00:20:15,500 --> 00:20:18,250
I could let you

436
00:20:18,625 --> 00:20:20,166
rent my uncle's place.

437
00:20:24,500 --> 00:20:26,833
One, two, three.

438
00:20:27,250 --> 00:20:29,625
One, two, three, I hate you.

439
00:20:30,500 --> 00:20:32,125
Why are you here?

440
00:20:32,375 --> 00:20:32,875
What?

441
00:20:32,875 --> 00:20:33,625
Don't ruin it.

442
00:20:33,626 --> 00:20:35,826
I finally graduated, can't I
enjoy pretending for once?

443
00:20:36,583 --> 00:20:39,374
Only you could make it
through college like that.

444
00:20:39,375 --> 00:20:40,749
It's fine, I finally graduated.

445
00:20:40,750 --> 00:20:42,749
I'm going to the south
with Xiao-Yu to be a civil servant.

446
00:20:42,750 --> 00:20:44,750
You should do your military service first.

447
00:20:44,875 --> 00:20:46,351
If you wait any longer, you'll be too old.

448
00:20:46,375 --> 00:20:48,624
Stop kissing, that's gross.

449
00:20:48,625 --> 00:20:50,125
Chia-Kai.

450
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:52,999
Professor.

451
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:55,458
Aren't you on maternity
leave? Why are you here?

452
00:20:56,041 --> 00:20:57,624
Such an important
turning point in your life,

453
00:20:57,625 --> 00:20:59,000
how could I miss it?

454
00:20:59,250 --> 00:21:00,875
And I was bored at home.

455
00:21:03,875 --> 00:21:06,500
Teacher, the line between you and your baby

456
00:21:07,250 --> 00:21:08,250
is so beautiful.

457
00:21:08,250 --> 00:21:09,250
How so?

458
00:21:09,875 --> 00:21:10,875
It feels

459
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:12,499
very colorful.

460
00:21:12,500 --> 00:21:13,500
Really?

461
00:21:13,501 --> 00:21:15,999
I've been doing prenatal education
very seriously every day.

462
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:17,249
When I talk to my baby,

463
00:21:17,250 --> 00:21:18,250
sometimes I'm a friend,

464
00:21:18,251 --> 00:21:19,374
sometimes a mom,

465
00:21:19,375 --> 00:21:20,624
sometimes a confidant,

466
00:21:20,625 --> 00:21:22,249
sometimes an enemy.

467
00:21:22,250 --> 00:21:24,665
He must feel like life in my
belly is full of excitement.

468
00:21:24,666 --> 00:21:27,124
You're such a unique mom, professor.

469
00:21:27,125 --> 00:21:28,624
Of course.

470
00:21:28,625 --> 00:21:30,499
I'm going to check on the other students
before I cry.

471
00:21:30,500 --> 00:21:32,458
Teacher, let's take a photo.

472
00:21:33,125 --> 00:21:36,250
Zeigarnik effect… I'll come find you later.

473
00:21:37,250 --> 00:21:37,875
See you later.

474
00:21:37,876 --> 00:21:39,000
See you.

475
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:43,083
Where's Da-Wei?

476
00:21:47,750 --> 00:21:48,750
Congrats on graduating.

477
00:21:49,375 --> 00:21:51,624
Grandma, sorry about earlier.

478
00:21:51,625 --> 00:21:54,624
I didn't have time to pick you up.

479
00:21:54,625 --> 00:21:57,250
Having Da-Wei pick me up is the same.

480
00:21:58,333 --> 00:21:59,333
Grandma.

481
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:03,207
My dear grandson Chia-Kai

482
00:22:03,208 --> 00:22:05,333
graduated today.

483
00:22:05,500 --> 00:22:06,957
Congratulations.

484
00:22:06,958 --> 00:22:07,958
Thank you, Grandma.

485
00:22:08,958 --> 00:22:10,333
Hug.

486
00:22:10,875 --> 00:22:14,500
Okay, one, two, three.

487
00:22:22,125 --> 00:22:23,999
Rock-paper-scissors.

488
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:25,875
Rock-paper-scissors.

489
00:22:26,250 --> 00:22:28,958
Shoot.

490
00:22:30,375 --> 00:22:31,625
How did I lose again?

491
00:22:32,125 --> 00:22:33,583
You're still

492
00:22:33,625 --> 00:22:34,875
too inexperienced.

493
00:22:35,708 --> 00:22:36,957
Next,

494
00:22:36,958 --> 00:22:38,957
we'll move

495
00:22:38,958 --> 00:22:42,457
this sofa…

496
00:22:42,458 --> 00:22:43,874
over here.

497
00:22:43,875 --> 00:22:46,249
Then we'll put the TV

498
00:22:46,250 --> 00:22:47,708
on this wall.

499
00:22:49,500 --> 00:22:50,583
A projector...

500
00:22:50,875 --> 00:22:52,750
we can even set up a projector.

501
00:22:57,375 --> 00:22:58,208
Perfect.

502
00:22:58,209 --> 00:22:59,458
But think about it,

503
00:22:59,875 --> 00:23:02,374
if we sit here and

504
00:23:02,375 --> 00:23:04,000
put the TV over there,

505
00:23:04,250 --> 00:23:05,708
wouldn't that be comfortable too?

506
00:23:07,125 --> 00:23:09,125
Let's try sitting.

507
00:23:10,875 --> 00:23:13,333
But then this wall would go to waste.

508
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:15,000
Not really.

509
00:23:15,250 --> 00:23:17,625
You could hang posters or something.

510
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:22,875
Don't you think the
walkway from the bathroom

511
00:23:23,125 --> 00:23:24,625
would feel too cramped?

512
00:23:25,250 --> 00:23:27,250
If you put the sofa there,

513
00:23:27,375 --> 00:23:28,875
wouldn't it still be cramped?

514
00:23:29,375 --> 00:23:30,250
And look,

515
00:23:30,251 --> 00:23:32,333
on a day like today,

516
00:23:32,375 --> 00:23:34,083
the sunlight comes right in.

517
00:23:34,125 --> 00:23:35,500
Isn't that nice?

518
00:23:38,583 --> 00:23:40,833
Let's pretend we're watching TV.

519
00:23:41,375 --> 00:23:43,500
I've got snacks in my hand,

520
00:23:43,750 --> 00:23:45,208
I can lean back here.

521
00:23:45,375 --> 00:23:46,583
Isn't that comfortable?

522
00:23:47,125 --> 00:23:48,833
- Here?
- Yeah.

523
00:23:49,250 --> 00:23:51,624
And if I want to lean somewhere else,

524
00:23:51,625 --> 00:23:53,041
I can do this.

525
00:23:55,375 --> 00:23:56,916
Not bad, right?

526
00:23:57,875 --> 00:24:01,458
I think you convinced me.

527
00:24:05,125 --> 00:24:06,125
So,

528
00:24:06,375 --> 00:24:07,458
what do you want to watch?

529
00:24:10,375 --> 00:24:11,500
A horror movie,

530
00:24:13,500 --> 00:24:14,625
a drama,

531
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:17,000
or…

532
00:24:17,001 --> 00:24:18,624
a romance?

533
00:24:18,625 --> 00:24:19,625
A romance.

534
00:24:27,250 --> 00:24:28,874
Don't do that on purpose.

535
00:24:28,875 --> 00:24:31,124
Don't drop crumbs.

536
00:24:31,125 --> 00:24:33,208
I know, I'll catch them.

537
00:24:34,500 --> 00:24:36,375
- Okay.
- Let's watch that one.

538
00:24:37,500 --> 00:24:39,041
This one?

539
00:24:39,500 --> 00:24:43,249
“Connecting to You”.

540
00:24:43,250 --> 00:24:44,625
Okay.

541
00:25:05,333 --> 00:25:06,749
Welcome to the two-minute
livestream on love.

542
00:25:06,750 --> 00:25:08,999
Don't blink or you'll miss!

543
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:11,332
This is going to be a sad one today,

544
00:25:11,333 --> 00:25:15,000
because I know a lot of
students are graduating

545
00:25:15,791 --> 00:25:17,624
and our little teacher

546
00:25:17,625 --> 00:25:18,915
is now all grown up

547
00:25:18,916 --> 00:25:20,249
and ready to face the world.

548
00:25:20,250 --> 00:25:21,790
So today, I'd like to talk about

549
00:25:21,791 --> 00:25:23,415
what we call

550
00:25:23,416 --> 00:25:25,082
in English

551
00:25:25,083 --> 00:25:26,665
the Principle of Scarcity.

552
00:25:26,666 --> 00:25:28,374
What it means is

553
00:25:28,375 --> 00:25:30,957
you want
whatever you can't get.

554
00:25:30,958 --> 00:25:32,040
So for example,

555
00:25:32,041 --> 00:25:34,165
if something is a limited edition,

556
00:25:34,166 --> 00:25:36,290
you automatically want it more.

557
00:25:36,291 --> 00:25:38,374
The same principle applies in love.

558
00:25:38,375 --> 00:25:40,207
If someone tells you

559
00:25:40,208 --> 00:25:42,040
that this secret is reserved for your ears only

560
00:25:42,041 --> 00:25:43,290
or that

561
00:25:43,291 --> 00:25:45,790
they've never felt this way
with anyone in their lives,

562
00:25:45,791 --> 00:25:46,957
only you.

563
00:25:46,958 --> 00:25:49,249
It's like today, our little teacher

564
00:25:49,250 --> 00:25:52,082
is down to his final episode

565
00:25:52,083 --> 00:25:55,499
and so everyone has shown up!

566
